---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SystemArchitecture from '../components/SystemArchitecture.astro';
import ProjectMedia from '../components/ProjectMedia.astro';
import StatusRail from '../components/StatusRail.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import ProfileSection from '../components/ProfileSection.astro';
import { personal } from '../data/personal';
import { project, heroMedia, laneMedia, historicalMedia, engineeringThemes } from '../data/autonomousDriving';
---
<BaseLayout title="Daniel Martínez | Autonomous-driving & robotics engineering" description={project.summary}>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="home-hero container">
      <div class="hero-kicker"><span>Engineering portfolio</span><span>CARLA / ROS2</span></div>
      <div class="hero-layout">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="identity">{personal.name}</p>
          <h1>Building an autonomy stack from <em>perception to routing.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-summary">A modular CARLA + ROS2 prototype: lane perception, temporal lane mapping and custom OpenDRIVE global routing.</p>
          <p class="ownership">{project.ownership}</p>
          <p class="hero-stage"><span>Global routing implemented</span><span>Route/lane association next</span></p>
          <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href={project.caseStudyPath}>Explore engineering case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={project.branchUrl}>View source ↗</a></div>
          <a class="hero-pdf" href={project.pdfPath} download>Download portfolio PDF ↓</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual"><div class="figure-index"><span>Autonomous Driving Laboratory</span></div><ProjectMedia media={heroMedia} priority /></div>
      </div>
      <StatusRail />
    </section>
    <section class="section architecture-section" id="architecture">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeader eyebrow="01 / System architecture" title="Two sources of knowledge. One explicit boundary." description="Local perception describes what the camera supports. Global routing describes where the map permits a route. Their connection is the next engineering milestone." />
        <SystemArchitecture />
        <div class="section-end"><p>LaneMap and RoutePlan own different IDs and revision semantics. Their planned association is geometric.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${project.caseStudyPath}#architecture`}>Inspect the contracts ↗</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="lane-evidence">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="editorial-heading"><SectionHeader eyebrow="02 / Current engineering evidence" title="Lane geometry that carries its uncertainty." /><div><p>Road markings become metric BEV geometry, filtered curves and temporal tracks. Ego-motion propagation and rolling memory preserve useful support without turning missing evidence into ground truth.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${project.caseStudyPath}#lane-stack`}>Inside the lane stack ↗</a></div></div>
        <ProjectMedia media={laneMedia} />
        <div class="evidence-footnote"><span class="mono-label">Observation → geometry → memory</span><p>Confidence, missing measurements and inferred boundaries remain explicit. An empty LaneMap can be a legitimate output.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section themes-section">
      <div class="container"><SectionHeader eyebrow="03 / Engineering approach" title="The work is in the boundaries." />
        <div class="theme-grid">{engineeringThemes.map((theme,index) => <article><span class="theme-index">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{theme.title}</h3><p>{theme.description}</p></article>)}</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="foundations">
      <div class="container foundations-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Earlier foundations</p><h2>The stack began<br /> with perception.</h2><p>Semantic segmentation and object tracking led to relative monocular depth, fusion, free space, occupancy and accumulated local mapping.</p><p class="muted">That earlier spatial stack remains real engineering history. Its accumulated occupancy grids are separate from today’s rolling vector LaneMap.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${project.caseStudyPath}#evolution`}>Follow the development ↗</a></div><ProjectMedia media={historicalMedia} /></div>
    </section>
    <section class="case-study-invitation container"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Engineering case study</p><a href={project.caseStudyPath}>From a camera frame<br /> to global route intent.<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p>Architecture, source contracts, development observations and the work still ahead.</p></section>
    <ProfileSection />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
